{"id":"9554b584e6760909","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-df-chow-group.md","title":"Chow Group","display":"df-chow-group — Chow Group","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-chow-group","aliases":["58-df-chow-group"],"display":"df-chow-group — Chow Group","depends_on":["[[../batch20/58-df-algebraic-cycle.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-chow-group"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-chow-group</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-chow-group — Chow Group"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"53a60793a214598a\" href=\"?note=53a60793a214598a\" title=\"../batch20/58-df-algebraic-cycle.md\">../batch20/58-df-algebraic-cycle.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,k_0,c,F,\\delta,G\\in V\\land n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land r\\in\\omega\">\\(X,k_0,c,F,\\delta,G\\in V\\land n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land r\\in\\omega\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal S^r_{k_0,n,c}(X),Z^r_{k_0,n,c}(X)\">\\(\\mathcal S^r_{k_0,n,c}(X),Z^r_{k_0,n,c}(X)\\)</span> (graded subvarieties and cycle group, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"53a60793a214598a\" href=\"?note=53a60793a214598a\" title=\"../batch20/58-df-algebraic-cycle.md\">../batch20/58-df-algebraic-cycle.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (set-function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ChowGroupData}_S\\subseteq V^8\">\\(\\mathrm{ChowGroupData}_S\\subseteq V^8\\)</span> (Chow quotient relative to explicit rational-function and divisor data, defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}chow-group} \\vdash \\mathrm{ChowGroupData}_S(G,X,k_0,n,c,r,F,\\delta)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(c,\\mathcal P(X),\\omega)\\land\\Bigl(\\bigl(r=0\\land G=Z^0_{k_0,n,c}(X)\\bigr)\\lor\\bigl(r&gt;0\\land\\mathrm{Function}(F,\\mathcal S^{r-1}_{k_0,n,c}(X),\\operatorname{ran}(F))\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\delta,\\{\\langle W,f\\rangle:W\\in\\mathcal S^{r-1}_{k_0,n,c}(X)\\land f\\in F(W)\\},Z^r_{k_0,n,c}(X))\\land G=Z^r_{k_0,n,c}(X)/\\langle\\operatorname{ran}(\\delta)\\rangle\\bigr)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}chow-group} \\vdash \\mathrm{ChowGroupData}_S(G,X,k_0,n,c,r,F,\\delta)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(c,\\mathcal P(X),\\omega)\\land\\Bigl(\\bigl(r=0\\land G=Z^0_{k_0,n,c}(X)\\bigr)\\lor\\bigl(r&gt;0\\land\\mathrm{Function}(F,\\mathcal S^{r-1}_{k_0,n,c}(X),\\operatorname{ran}(F))\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\delta,\\{\\langle W,f\\rangle:W\\in\\mathcal S^{r-1}_{k_0,n,c}(X)\\land f\\in F(W)\\},Z^r_{k_0,n,c}(X))\\land G=Z^r_{k_0,n,c}(X)/\\langle\\operatorname{ran}(\\delta)\\rangle\\bigr)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The upstream cycle atom requires the field, ambient dimension, and codimension map, so all of them are retained in the signature here.</li>\n<li>The rational-function family <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span> and principal-divisor map <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta\">\\(\\delta\\)</span> are explicit inputs.  The knowledge base has no compatible higher-codimension rational-equivalence atom from which they could be inferred.</li>\n<li>At codimension <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0\">\\(0\\)</span> there are no codimension-<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(-1)\">\\((-1)\\)</span> subvarieties, so the quotient is the cycle group itself.</li>\n<li>Bloch's formula: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"CH^i(X) \\otimes \\mathbb{Q} \\cong H^i(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)\">\\(CH^i(X) \\otimes \\mathbb{Q} \\cong H^i(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Higher Chow groups <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"CH^p(X, q)\">\\(CH^p(X, q)\\)</span> relate to motivic cohomology.</li>\n<li>Suslin conjecture: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"CH^i(X) \\otimes \\mathbb{Q} \\cong H^i_{\\mathcal{M}}(X, \\mathbb{Q}(i))\">\\(CH^i(X) \\otimes \\mathbb{Q} \\cong H^i_{\\mathcal{M}}(X, \\mathbb{Q}(i))\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch20/58-df-algebraic-cycle.md","status":"resolved","id":"53a60793a214598a","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-algebraic-cycle.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch20/58-df-algebraic-cycle.md","status":"resolved","id":"53a60793a214598a","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathcal S^r_{k_0,n,c}(X),Z^r_{k_0,n,c}(X)$ (graded subvarieties and cycle group, see [[../batch20/58-df-algebraic-cycle.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3$ (set-function predicate, see [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,k_0,c,F,\\delta,G\\in V\\land n\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land r\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathcal S^r_{k_0,n,c}(X),Z^r_{k_0,n,c}(X)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ChowGroupData}_S\\subseteq V^8","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}chow-group} \\vdash \\mathrm{ChowGroupData}_S(G,X,k_0,n,c,r,F,\\delta)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Function}(c,\\mathcal P(X),\\omega)\\land\\Bigl(\\bigl(r=0\\land G=Z^0_{k_0,n,c}(X)\\bigr)\\lor\\bigl(r>0\\land\\mathrm{Function}(F,\\mathcal S^{r-1}_{k_0,n,c}(X),\\operatorname{ran}(F))\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\delta,\\{\\langle W,f\\rangle:W\\in\\mathcal S^{r-1}_{k_0,n,c}(X)\\land f\\in F(W)\\},Z^r_{k_0,n,c}(X))\\land G=Z^r_{k_0,n,c}(X)/\\langle\\operatorname{ran}(\\delta)\\rangle\\bigr)\\Bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"F","display":false},{"tex":"\\delta","display":false},{"tex":"0","display":false},{"tex":"(-1)","display":false},{"tex":"CH^i(X) \\otimes \\mathbb{Q} \\cong H^i(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)","display":false},{"tex":"CH^p(X, q)","display":false},{"tex":"CH^i(X) \\otimes \\mathbb{Q} \\cong H^i_{\\mathcal{M}}(X, \\mathbb{Q}(i))","display":false}],"bytes":1956,"backlinks":[{"id":"3311bfe05245f437","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"The four algebraic-geometry interface predicates name the standard constructions at the resolution currently available in this book.  In particular, [[58-df-chow-group]] is an affine/codimension presentation with external divisor data and does not by itself define projective $CH_0(X)^0$; this theorem no longer pretends that its zero-argument notation does so."},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-277","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-chow-group.md|58-df-chow-group]]（batch08）"}],"outgoing":["53a60793a214598a","36d7463d215be751"]}